1
00:00:00,018 --> 00:00:01,499
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,041
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:05,500
(Episode 77)

4
00:00:06,416 --> 00:00:08,749
Look for a place to rent.
I'll pay the deposit.

5
00:00:09,329 --> 00:00:10,432
Okay.

6
00:00:10,518 --> 00:00:13,000
Make sure it's big enough.

7
00:00:13,041 --> 00:00:14,708
You'll need room for a baby soon.

8
00:00:15,724 --> 00:00:17,458
What? Is something bothering you?

9
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,163
Should we buy them a place instead?

10
00:00:22,375 --> 00:00:26,916
I don't mind,
as long as no unwelcome guest moves in.

11
00:00:27,390 --> 00:00:29,973
Whether you rent or buy is up to you.

12
00:00:30,186 --> 00:00:31,395
What unwelcome guest?

13
00:00:31,397 --> 00:00:33,750
Why talk like that to your own in-law?

14
00:00:33,791 --> 00:00:35,416
Don't call me your in-law.

15
00:00:36,291 --> 00:00:37,541
Mom, that's out of line.

16
00:00:37,583 --> 00:00:39,626
That's why I said I wouldn't come.

17
00:00:39,965 --> 00:00:42,382
I've never eaten with a mistress before.

18
00:00:42,732 --> 00:00:45,277
Honey, you made a promise. Keep it.

19
00:00:45,916 --> 00:00:48,535
We never registered our marriage,

20
00:00:48,666 --> 00:00:53,076
but when he passed away,
Seung Hyun and I arranged his funeral.

21
00:00:53,623 --> 00:00:55,706
My arm hurts too much to play cello now,

22
00:00:55,727 --> 00:00:59,310
but people used to say
I was the best at what I did.

23
00:00:59,496 --> 00:01:02,413
You know I still work hard, right?

24
00:01:02,515 --> 00:01:05,015
Of course. You're very impressive.

25
00:01:05,376 --> 00:01:08,126
I've never seen an in-law
brag at a family meeting before.

26
00:01:09,092 --> 00:01:12,333
I'm sorry to interrupt. Mother...

27
00:01:15,260 --> 00:01:17,089
I'd like to live with you.

28
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,875
Live where, Ji Ni?

29
00:01:22,588 --> 00:01:25,505
No. Who said you could live with us?

30
00:01:25,625 --> 00:01:29,223
Dad, we were going to live on our own,
but not with things the way they are.

31
00:01:29,451 --> 00:01:31,951
Let us live with you as Uncle did,
even if it's just for a year.

32
00:01:32,875 --> 00:01:34,572
No, that's not right.

33
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,248
Please let us.

34
00:01:36,297 --> 00:01:39,797
Really? So that's what you had in mind.

35
00:01:40,291 --> 00:01:41,542
I don't want that.

36
00:01:42,098 --> 00:01:43,223
Okay.

37
00:01:43,687 --> 00:01:46,777
I won't go to their place.
Please let them live on their own.

38
00:01:47,666 --> 00:01:50,234
I've been a burden to Ji Ni all her life.

39
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:52,747
You're all going too far.

40
00:01:53,750 --> 00:01:55,545
I won't visit. Get a place of your own.

41
00:01:55,546 --> 00:01:56,868
Why move in with them?

42
00:01:57,098 --> 00:01:59,060
You two go live happily on your own.

43
00:01:59,829 --> 00:02:02,326
I won't visit. I mean it.

44
00:02:02,812 --> 00:02:07,041
Wait, Mom!

45
00:02:08,416 --> 00:02:11,291
Look at the bride's brother,
running back and forth.

46
00:02:17,041 --> 00:02:20,625
Mom, you can't just walk out like that.

47
00:02:20,666 --> 00:02:23,333
You silly girl.
Why would you live with them?

48
00:02:23,416 --> 00:02:26,000
Tell them I won't come over
so you two can get your own place.

49
00:02:26,041 --> 00:02:28,000
I can visit after that.

50
00:02:29,431 --> 00:02:32,556
Who does she think she is,
trying to come between us?

51
00:02:32,583 --> 00:02:34,708
Now hurry back inside.

52
00:02:34,836 --> 00:02:37,541
Hey, why are you out here too?

53
00:02:37,707 --> 00:02:41,373
Get back in there and finish the meeting.
You're her oldest brother.

54
00:02:41,375 --> 00:02:45,458
Hurry, get back inside. Go on.

55
00:02:53,583 --> 00:02:56,458
(Pumseonggak)

56
00:03:11,125 --> 00:03:14,083
Right. Aren't they just the best?

57
00:03:14,250 --> 00:03:19,125
They sure think they're the best.

58
00:03:19,541 --> 00:03:21,203
That crazy woman.

59
00:03:21,453 --> 00:03:25,495
I'll make sure she never sees
her son again.

60
00:03:27,139 --> 00:03:29,181
Does she think she can walk all over me?

61
00:03:37,750 --> 00:03:38,791
Ma'am!

62
00:03:39,416 --> 00:03:41,735
Who are you calling "ma'am"?

63
00:03:42,541 --> 00:03:45,166
It's me. I guess you don't recognize me.

64
00:03:45,528 --> 00:03:47,903
What's wrong with you? Are you crazy?

65
00:03:48,375 --> 00:03:51,791
Remember me? From Pumseonggak?

66
00:03:55,625 --> 00:03:57,583
Pumseonggak?

67
00:03:59,246 --> 00:04:01,079
You're the one who told me to run away.

68
00:04:17,250 --> 00:04:18,958
That was you?

69
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,337
Now you remember, right?

70
00:04:20,338 --> 00:04:22,208
I've been trying so hard to find you.

71
00:04:24,538 --> 00:04:25,579
Who is this?

72
00:04:28,588 --> 00:04:29,672
Are you okay?

73
00:04:29,871 --> 00:04:33,121
Yes. Why'd you come out? Where's Ji Ni?

74
00:04:33,125 --> 00:04:34,541
They're discussing where to live.

75
00:04:34,825 --> 00:04:36,950
- I didn't think they needed me.
- Okay.

76
00:04:38,390 --> 00:04:41,765
He used to take lessons from me.

77
00:04:41,916 --> 00:04:45,416
It's been a long time. Thanks for today.

78
00:05:05,041 --> 00:05:07,305
You're still full of secrets.

79
00:05:08,247 --> 00:05:11,164
You're really from the family
that ran Pumseonggak?

80
00:05:11,241 --> 00:05:12,658
Yes.

81
00:05:13,653 --> 00:05:15,778
But you haven't aged at all.

82
00:05:16,450 --> 00:05:19,408
Are you a model now?
You're in that game commercial, right?

83
00:05:20,208 --> 00:05:21,666
You saw that commercial?

84
00:05:23,414 --> 00:05:24,789
Why did you want to find me?

85
00:05:24,829 --> 00:05:27,538
My mom and dad died because of you.

86
00:05:27,788 --> 00:05:29,253
What are you talking about?

87
00:05:29,451 --> 00:05:31,867
I never saw your parents after that day.

88
00:05:32,039 --> 00:05:33,081
Exactly.

89
00:05:35,583 --> 00:05:37,750
(Pumseonggak, Traditional Chinese Cuisine)

90
00:05:46,664 --> 00:05:48,914
Look at this. You have a son, right?

91
00:05:48,982 --> 00:05:53,024
No, my son can't ride a motorcycle.

92
00:05:53,031 --> 00:05:54,573
I told the police that already.

93
00:05:54,692 --> 00:05:57,013
We didn't have any deliveries that day,

94
00:05:57,138 --> 00:05:59,937
and nobody took the motorcycle out.

95
00:06:00,775 --> 00:06:05,166
I saw it. A yellow basket behind my car.

96
00:06:05,208 --> 00:06:06,916
No, that's not true.

97
00:06:07,097 --> 00:06:09,389
It's okay. I came to help you.

98
00:06:09,958 --> 00:06:13,916
I'll keep quiet, but you need to leave.
Don't get caught.

99
00:06:14,293 --> 00:06:18,793
What? But this is our hometown...

100
00:06:18,861 --> 00:06:20,528
Do you want to ruin your son's life?

101
00:06:20,890 --> 00:06:22,848
Do you know how scary that old man is?

102
00:06:23,025 --> 00:06:24,914
Shut down the restaurant and leave now.

103
00:06:24,916 --> 00:06:30,017
We're so deep in debt
that we can't afford to move...

104
00:06:31,973 --> 00:06:34,807
I'll help you. Just go into hiding.

105
00:06:34,833 --> 00:06:37,333
Why would you go this far for us?

106
00:06:38,870 --> 00:06:41,620
So that old man never gets any peace,

107
00:06:43,412 --> 00:06:46,203
and that mother suffers her whole life.

108
00:06:52,005 --> 00:06:55,047
So what's your problem?

109
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:57,525
You didn't get caught.
You had a good life thanks to me.

110
00:06:57,672 --> 00:07:00,058
Someone's leg was ruined because of you.

111
00:07:02,041 --> 00:07:03,221
A good life?

112
00:07:03,489 --> 00:07:05,938
My parents were scared all the time,

113
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,750
and once we moved the restaurant,
we barely got any customers.

114
00:07:09,248 --> 00:07:11,081
My whole family fell apart.

115
00:07:11,838 --> 00:07:14,963
Dad kept saying,
"I should've turned myself in."

116
00:07:15,557 --> 00:07:16,968
Then why didn't he?

117
00:07:17,113 --> 00:07:18,958
None of you wanted to.

118
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,390
Because we took the money.

119
00:07:20,904 --> 00:07:23,333
Mom said taking the money
meant we had to keep quiet.

120
00:07:26,701 --> 00:07:28,742
Pay me, or I'll turn myself in right now.

121
00:07:29,085 --> 00:07:31,001
And I'll drag you into it too.

122
00:07:31,729 --> 00:07:33,604
I'll say you stopped me from confessing.

123
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:35,260
Go ahead.

124
00:07:36,001 --> 00:07:38,302
The statute of limitations
expired years ago.

125
00:07:40,284 --> 00:07:42,234
Do you think it's expired
for that family too?

126
00:07:43,691 --> 00:07:47,899
So give me money. Money!

127
00:07:48,361 --> 00:07:50,653
Hey, let go!

128
00:07:57,750 --> 00:08:00,166
Hey! Give it back!

129
00:08:05,005 --> 00:08:06,095
Na Se Ri.

130
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:09,463
You'll be hearing from me more often now.

131
00:08:10,708 --> 00:08:12,625
Why would I talk to you?

132
00:08:14,173 --> 00:08:16,756
Thanks, ma'am. I'll call you.

133
00:08:46,307 --> 00:08:47,695
That damn old man...

134
00:08:48,762 --> 00:08:50,352
Yeong Ju...

135
00:08:55,444 --> 00:08:58,653
I felt so much resentment back then.

136
00:09:01,710 --> 00:09:05,918
If only he'd done the paperwork.
That damn paperwork...

137
00:09:17,538 --> 00:09:19,246
They're getting married any day now...

138
00:09:26,172 --> 00:09:30,088
Seriously, why does she want
to move in with us?

139
00:09:30,163 --> 00:09:32,496
She'd have to live by her in-laws' rules.

140
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:35,973
- Honey.
- These days, it's the in-laws who suffer.

141
00:09:36,041 --> 00:09:39,833
You're back. How did it go?

142
00:09:39,941 --> 00:09:41,732
We've decided to live here, Aunt.

143
00:09:41,790 --> 00:09:43,748
Really? That's great.

144
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:46,333
See? They're all on the same side.

145
00:09:46,416 --> 00:09:49,583
Honey, I'll be the only one left out.

146
00:09:49,625 --> 00:09:51,548
The kids are being so thoughtful.

147
00:09:51,549 --> 00:09:53,166
Let's take them in for just a few months.

148
00:09:53,208 --> 00:09:54,980
I told you, it's my dream.

149
00:09:55,009 --> 00:09:57,827
My dream is to have three men
and three women in this house.

150
00:09:59,878 --> 00:10:03,134
I really have no one on my side.

151
00:10:08,622 --> 00:10:11,206
Dad, I'll do better. I'm sorry.

152
00:10:11,248 --> 00:10:13,456
You can't just look after your own woman.

153
00:10:13,515 --> 00:10:15,182
You have to look after mine too, okay?

154
00:10:15,875 --> 00:10:16,916
Okay, Dad.

155
00:10:17,101 --> 00:10:19,351
Your jokes are hilarious, Joong Bin.

156
00:10:19,583 --> 00:10:21,337
Thank you for laughing.

157
00:10:21,338 --> 00:10:22,541
Are you heading out?

158
00:10:22,625 --> 00:10:25,338
Yes, I need to go keep my son in line too.

159
00:10:25,339 --> 00:10:26,875
I'll be back before dinner.

160
00:10:27,083 --> 00:10:29,000
- Okay. Take care.
- Okay.

161
00:10:30,666 --> 00:10:33,375
Aunt, I'll give you a ride. I have to go
to the publishing house anyway.

162
00:10:33,416 --> 00:10:34,625
Sure. Let's go.

163
00:10:45,708 --> 00:10:47,181
I'm not hungry.

164
00:10:47,708 --> 00:10:49,158
Eat anyway.

165
00:10:50,083 --> 00:10:52,364
Eat now, sleep at night,
and work during the day.

166
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:02,742
You quit the station over that crazy woman
and got depressed.

167
00:11:02,925 --> 00:11:06,382
Then you felt sorry for that goblin girl,
defended her, and got depressed again.

168
00:11:08,461 --> 00:11:09,575
Goblin...

169
00:11:10,501 --> 00:11:13,500
That's it. I was bewitched by a goblin.

170
00:11:15,958 --> 00:11:18,526
You're going to ruin your life
over a woman.

171
00:11:18,718 --> 00:11:20,666
I'm so sick of it.

172
00:11:20,875 --> 00:11:25,958
I can forget a husband like him,
but I can't forget the child.

173
00:11:26,083 --> 00:11:28,155
I'm telling you, that's not it.

174
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:31,083
Just trust me. I'm simply feeling down.

175
00:11:33,041 --> 00:11:35,083
I get like this sometimes.

176
00:11:36,625 --> 00:11:38,930
Every time, you try to find the cause
and fix everything.

177
00:11:39,195 --> 00:11:40,696
How many times have I told you not to?

178
00:11:40,708 --> 00:11:43,500
If you keep this up, I'll move out.
I'm serious.

179
00:11:43,541 --> 00:11:45,750
Go ahead. I'd be relieved too.

180
00:11:47,923 --> 00:11:50,048
Marriage has made you pretty tough.

181
00:11:50,918 --> 00:11:52,210
Don't worry.

182
00:11:52,916 --> 00:11:57,458
I need to plan my next project,
but I can't think or concentrate.

183
00:11:57,833 --> 00:12:00,500
I'm depressed, wondering
what I've done with my life.

184
00:12:00,916 --> 00:12:04,088
So stop badmouthing that girl.
She's already gone to England.

185
00:12:04,210 --> 00:12:05,710
Even when I forget her,
you remind me of her.

186
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,244
I'm serious.

187
00:12:08,645 --> 00:12:11,293
It's my problem. Mine alone.

188
00:12:11,625 --> 00:12:15,655
I'm not starved for affection,
so stop worrying.

189
00:12:16,422 --> 00:12:18,547
I'm more worried
about you worrying about me.

190
00:12:22,404 --> 00:12:23,445
Eat.

191
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:32,648
Don't pressure him too much.
Give him time.

192
00:12:32,715 --> 00:12:34,248
He says he's working on a project.

193
00:12:34,260 --> 00:12:35,427
Okay.

194
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:39,408
At least he comes out, eats, and talks
when you visit.

195
00:12:39,541 --> 00:12:40,916
He doesn't talk to you?

196
00:12:40,958 --> 00:12:42,136
Not really.

197
00:12:55,871 --> 00:12:58,833
Pumseonggak? What's this?

198
00:12:59,047 --> 00:13:00,814
It's the motorcycle that hit Seung Woo.

199
00:13:01,043 --> 00:13:06,251
I was told it was a delivery motorcycle
from Pumseonggak, a Chinese restaurant.

200
00:13:07,229 --> 00:13:09,812
How did you find that out?

201
00:13:10,289 --> 00:13:14,914
Grandpa checked every Chinese restaurant
in the area. Didn't he check this one?

202
00:13:14,944 --> 00:13:15,944
He did.

203
00:13:16,190 --> 00:13:21,757
But when I reviewed the records,
they only questioned the delivery drivers.

204
00:13:22,242 --> 00:13:24,617
They never checked the owner's son.

205
00:13:24,829 --> 00:13:26,372
- The son?
- Yes.

206
00:13:26,538 --> 00:13:29,789
Back then, he never even went
to high school.

207
00:13:29,914 --> 00:13:32,121
He used to ride
the restaurant's delivery motorcycle.

208
00:13:32,422 --> 00:13:33,672
And he didn't have a license.

209
00:13:34,208 --> 00:13:37,060
Where did you hear all this?

210
00:13:37,291 --> 00:13:39,125
Why are we only hearing about this now?

211
00:13:39,166 --> 00:13:43,400
So I went to the place Pumseonggak
moved to right after the accident.

212
00:13:47,885 --> 00:13:49,003
This is the place.

213
00:13:49,662 --> 00:13:51,907
They moved again 20 years ago.

214
00:13:51,973 --> 00:13:55,015
There's no record
of where they went after that.

215
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:57,873
We need to find out where they live now.

216
00:13:57,902 --> 00:13:59,649
Let's find them
and get to the bottom of this.

217
00:14:00,567 --> 00:14:04,567
We have to find whoever ruined
someone else's child's life...

218
00:14:05,444 --> 00:14:07,440
and has been hiding all these years,
then make them pay.

219
00:14:07,668 --> 00:14:10,251
I'll get my revenge.

220
00:14:10,499 --> 00:14:13,536
But the statute of limitations
has expired.

221
00:14:14,053 --> 00:14:15,790
They might not face much punishment.

222
00:14:16,416 --> 00:14:17,875
I still need to know the truth.

223
00:14:18,166 --> 00:14:21,625
I'll grab them by the collar
and make them apologize.

224
00:14:26,750 --> 00:14:29,875
But how on earth did you
find all this out?

225
00:14:32,761 --> 00:14:33,803
Well...

226
00:14:42,291 --> 00:14:43,879
What did you decide about the house?

227
00:14:50,567 --> 00:14:52,358
I decided to move in.

228
00:14:53,079 --> 00:14:54,246
I'm sorry, Mom.

229
00:14:54,672 --> 00:14:56,127
I was too selfish.

230
00:14:56,297 --> 00:14:58,404
I should've talked it over with you.

231
00:14:58,625 --> 00:14:59,963
You must've been upset.

232
00:15:00,265 --> 00:15:03,057
No, you did the right thing.
It's a good decision.

233
00:15:03,816 --> 00:15:06,441
Stay there with Ji Hu,
where you'll be safe.

234
00:15:06,458 --> 00:15:08,833
And don't come anywhere near Seo Chon.

235
00:15:09,125 --> 00:15:11,916
Come on. I'm apologizing. I'm sorry.

236
00:15:11,986 --> 00:15:15,146
I'm not giving you a hard time.
I really think you did the right thing.

237
00:15:15,873 --> 00:15:17,998
I should find a place
and move out soon too.

238
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,416
With you gone, I don't have the energy
to stay here.

239
00:15:32,458 --> 00:15:34,458
I've pushed myself too hard for too long.

240
00:15:35,347 --> 00:15:36,389
Na Se Ri!

241
00:15:39,203 --> 00:15:41,773
I'll leave you two alone. Go ahead.

242
00:15:45,982 --> 00:15:49,665
Yeong Ju, I'm having a really hard time.
Can we talk later?

243
00:15:49,666 --> 00:15:53,583
Did you go around claiming to be
my son's mom to keep the witness quiet?

244
00:15:54,795 --> 00:15:56,138
Not this again.

245
00:15:56,359 --> 00:15:58,583
I honestly thought she was a con artist.

246
00:15:58,625 --> 00:16:01,937
Who are you to judge
whether she's a con artist?

247
00:16:02,333 --> 00:16:05,499
You drove off that day.
What would you know about it?

248
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:09,208
That's right. I drove off.

249
00:16:09,708 --> 00:16:12,791
And I've felt guilty about it ever since.

250
00:16:13,083 --> 00:16:16,541
But when I actually met her,
Pumseonggak was all she knew.

251
00:16:16,583 --> 00:16:19,625
You don't realize
how important that clue is.

252
00:16:20,541 --> 00:16:23,095
That's a clue?

253
00:16:24,123 --> 00:16:25,831
So have you found out anything?

254
00:16:25,833 --> 00:16:28,083
Seung Hyun's trying to find the address
of the house they moved to.

255
00:16:28,291 --> 00:16:32,250
I heard the son never went to high school
and rode a delivery motorcycle.

256
00:16:32,583 --> 00:16:33,833
Still think that's useless information?

257
00:16:33,875 --> 00:16:36,773
Yeong Ju, the statute of limitations
has expired.

258
00:16:36,791 --> 00:16:38,392
There's no statute of limitations on lies.

259
00:16:39,116 --> 00:16:42,783
Even if we catch and kill that person,
it won't give Seung Woo his leg back.

260
00:16:43,877 --> 00:16:46,752
But they will be punished.
Don't get involved.

261
00:16:47,162 --> 00:16:49,203
Okay. I was wrong.

262
00:16:55,695 --> 00:16:57,949
I was going to take care of your paperwork
and then leave.

263
00:16:58,653 --> 00:17:00,523
I'd already talked things over
with Grandpa.

264
00:17:01,708 --> 00:17:04,791
I was planning to study abroad again
and pursue my field.

265
00:17:05,208 --> 00:17:06,291
What?

266
00:17:06,787 --> 00:17:08,324
But then the accident happened.

267
00:17:09,451 --> 00:17:11,802
Who could I leave him with
after he lost his leg and grew so fragile?

268
00:17:11,803 --> 00:17:13,087
So I couldn't leave.

269
00:17:14,625 --> 00:17:19,083
If not for the accident, you'd have become
his official wife much sooner.

270
00:17:20,039 --> 00:17:21,608
My goodness!

271
00:17:22,028 --> 00:17:25,289
Yeong Ju, why are you telling me this now?

272
00:17:25,291 --> 00:17:26,831
What difference would it make if I did?

273
00:17:27,722 --> 00:17:30,920
You said you didn't see the accident.
You know nothing about what happened.

274
00:17:31,472 --> 00:17:34,755
He was his dad, yet he didn't even notice
his own child falling.

275
00:17:35,348 --> 00:17:37,015
I hated Cha Min Ki the most.

276
00:17:38,791 --> 00:17:43,916
Yeong Ju, why are you telling me
all this now?

277
00:17:43,958 --> 00:17:46,333
I had no idea.

278
00:17:46,916 --> 00:17:49,431
Anyway, take this as a warning.
Stay out of it.

279
00:18:10,583 --> 00:18:16,250
Fine. I'll just focus on the wedding.

280
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:18,644
Then I'll leave.

281
00:18:52,043 --> 00:18:55,835
Ji Hu, can you meet me for a moment?

282
00:18:58,208 --> 00:19:01,416
I told you I have no appetite.

283
00:19:04,125 --> 00:19:05,125
Mom.

284
00:19:07,338 --> 00:19:11,207
I used to love it when you did this,
but not anymore.

285
00:19:11,675 --> 00:19:13,340
Your flattery isn't sincere.

286
00:19:14,816 --> 00:19:17,094
I'm not flattering you, Mom. I mean it.

287
00:19:17,666 --> 00:19:19,791
Have a drink, too.

288
00:19:20,866 --> 00:19:22,543
You barely ate anything earlier, either.

289
00:19:22,748 --> 00:19:25,498
I really need to learn some self-control.

290
00:19:25,547 --> 00:19:26,547
Sure.

291
00:19:26,675 --> 00:19:29,557
The happiness of the two men
in this house is in your hands.

292
00:19:29,833 --> 00:19:31,666
That's all talk.

293
00:19:31,791 --> 00:19:34,083
Ji Ni's mom is coming. Come on, let's eat.

294
00:19:34,583 --> 00:19:38,208
She stormed out so rudely before.
Why is she coming back now?

295
00:19:38,607 --> 00:19:40,066
I really can't stand her.

296
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:41,333
Mom.

297
00:19:44,463 --> 00:19:46,338
I guess she's here.

298
00:19:47,375 --> 00:19:49,291
Just when we're about to eat again.

299
00:19:50,079 --> 00:19:52,079
Our timing never works out.

300
00:19:54,256 --> 00:19:57,881
I was thoughtless earlier. I'm sorry.

301
00:19:57,958 --> 00:20:00,516
Is that why you came? To apologize?

302
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:03,315
That, and...

303
00:20:04,021 --> 00:20:08,242
if the kids are going to live here,
there's not much to prepare.

304
00:20:08,357 --> 00:20:12,857
I thought the two of you could just agree
on a suitable date.

305
00:20:13,041 --> 00:20:14,625
I just wanted to...

306
00:20:16,547 --> 00:20:18,463
do my part as a mother.

307
00:20:19,291 --> 00:20:21,016
You really didn't have to go this far.

308
00:20:21,583 --> 00:20:25,166
I understand how hard it is
to give away your precious daughter.

309
00:20:25,916 --> 00:20:27,105
Thank you.

310
00:20:28,083 --> 00:20:33,041
I feel so lonely arranging
such a big occasion without my husband.

311
00:20:33,875 --> 00:20:35,028
Mother.

312
00:20:44,083 --> 00:20:46,000
One hundred thousand dollars? Honey.

313
00:20:48,247 --> 00:20:49,664
You really didn't have to...

314
00:20:49,666 --> 00:20:53,860
No, just please be kind to my dear Ji Ni.

315
00:20:54,958 --> 00:20:58,333
If her dad were still alive,
this would be nothing.

316
00:20:58,375 --> 00:21:01,547
He's our only son, so this is our first
and last wedding as parents.

317
00:21:01,747 --> 00:21:04,414
We'll make sure everything
is done properly, so please don't worry.

318
00:21:04,416 --> 00:21:05,458
Okay.

319
00:21:06,166 --> 00:21:09,681
We'll send the wedding gift money
with Ji Hu.

320
00:21:11,375 --> 00:21:15,691
But aren't you staying
at someone else's place right now?

321
00:21:17,458 --> 00:21:19,072
As I told you,

322
00:21:20,063 --> 00:21:23,375
if my husband were alive
and my business hadn't failed,

323
00:21:23,916 --> 00:21:26,336
I could've even bought you diamonds.

324
00:21:26,337 --> 00:21:29,754
That was all I ever dreamed of.

325
00:21:30,333 --> 00:21:34,791
I worked myself to the bone
to support my husband and daughter.

326
00:21:35,708 --> 00:21:37,583
She always finds a way to brag.

327
00:21:38,125 --> 00:21:40,000
- Listen, Se Ri.
- Well...

328
00:21:40,333 --> 00:21:43,583
We'll take good care
of your precious daughter.

329
00:21:44,125 --> 00:21:45,166
Thank you.

330
00:21:46,519 --> 00:21:48,914
I'm counting on you.
Please take good care of her.

331
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:50,625
Of course, Mother. Don't worry.

332
00:21:52,083 --> 00:21:53,708
How sweet.

333
00:22:02,416 --> 00:22:05,141
This is the watch
Ji Ni's dad used to wear. Is it okay?

334
00:22:05,143 --> 00:22:06,217
Of course.

335
00:22:06,352 --> 00:22:09,492
Since it belonged to Ji Ni's dad,
I'll treasure it.

336
00:22:09,645 --> 00:22:10,687
Good.

337
00:22:12,297 --> 00:22:17,096
But it might be a little cramped
for the two of you.

338
00:22:18,422 --> 00:22:20,572
It's fine. There's a living room too.

339
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:23,000
I'll be at work,
and my dear Ji Ni will be at her studio.

340
00:22:23,206 --> 00:22:26,123
"Your dear Ji Ni?"
Have you two gotten that close?

341
00:22:26,182 --> 00:22:29,265
Well, that took you long enough.

342
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:36,792
Thank you, Mother, for being
so accommodating about the house.

343
00:22:37,807 --> 00:22:40,390
But wasn't the wedding gift money
too much for you?

344
00:22:41,047 --> 00:22:42,186
No.

345
00:22:42,626 --> 00:22:45,630
I'd already set some money aside
for Ji Ni's wedding.

346
00:22:46,208 --> 00:22:47,333
Be happy together.

347
00:22:48,973 --> 00:22:50,182
Are you very upset?

348
00:22:51,095 --> 00:22:52,886
You seem a little...

349
00:22:53,625 --> 00:22:55,944
No, I'm just tired.

350
00:22:56,375 --> 00:22:59,450
I've said what I came to say.
I'll get going. Get some rest.

351
00:23:00,583 --> 00:23:04,666
Please think of me as your son, Mother.

352
00:23:05,041 --> 00:23:06,416
And don't feel lonely.

353
00:23:07,750 --> 00:23:08,791
Okay.

354
00:23:09,875 --> 00:23:11,146
My dear Ji Ni...

355
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:15,329
has had such a hard time
since her dad died. You know that, right?

356
00:23:15,958 --> 00:23:18,291
I know. I'll take even better care of her.

357
00:23:20,166 --> 00:23:24,250
And make sure you get a wedding ring
with a big diamond.

358
00:23:24,291 --> 00:23:26,541
You're not buying a house after all.
Got it?

359
00:23:27,333 --> 00:23:28,375
Yes.

360
00:23:30,166 --> 00:23:31,208
Take care.

361
00:23:31,250 --> 00:23:33,166
You too. Get some rest.

362
00:24:01,289 --> 00:24:04,539
Bride and groom, let's go
over your reservation details.

363
00:24:04,541 --> 00:24:06,664
Your guaranteed guest count is 200.

364
00:24:06,666 --> 00:24:09,207
And after you walk down the aisle,

365
00:24:09,208 --> 00:24:12,375
we can shower you with confetti.
It'll look beautiful.

366
00:24:13,367 --> 00:24:14,659
- Thank you.
- It'll be gorgeous.

367
00:24:19,791 --> 00:24:20,890
Come on in.

368
00:24:22,333 --> 00:24:23,333
It's beautiful.

369
00:24:23,458 --> 00:24:25,833
Would you like to give it a try?
Feel free to walk around.

370
00:24:43,014 --> 00:24:47,222
Mom, could you walk me down the aisle
tomorrow?

371
00:24:47,386 --> 00:24:48,970
I'm scared to walk in alone.

372
00:24:49,125 --> 00:24:51,268
Scared? What are you scared of?

373
00:24:52,291 --> 00:24:55,260
I'll just stay quietly in the background.

374
00:24:56,069 --> 00:24:59,862
Forget your dad and me.
Just keep your eyes on Ji Hu as you walk.

375
00:25:00,250 --> 00:25:06,041
Now you're going to build
a proper family of your own.

376
00:25:06,547 --> 00:25:07,755
And make sure you register the marriage.

377
00:25:12,541 --> 00:25:15,833
I have no regrets now,
my wonderful daughter.

378
00:25:20,519 --> 00:25:22,303
I'm sorry for causing you so much trouble.

379
00:25:22,572 --> 00:25:24,361
You cried a lot because of me, didn't you?

380
00:25:24,791 --> 00:25:26,708
You cried even more than I did.

381
00:25:27,583 --> 00:25:30,083
I'm the one who should be sorry.

382
00:25:31,333 --> 00:25:36,583
I wanted to hold your hand
and walk you to school,

383
00:25:37,025 --> 00:25:39,567
and go to your sports days with you.

384
00:25:45,833 --> 00:25:47,541
It must have been hard for you.

385
00:25:49,557 --> 00:25:54,723
Thank you for bringing me here to live
and helping me meet my brothers.

386
00:25:55,666 --> 00:25:57,000
You figured it out?

387
00:25:57,833 --> 00:25:59,614
Not at first.

388
00:26:00,375 --> 00:26:03,664
I thought you were being ridiculous,
so I wanted to move out quickly.

389
00:26:05,875 --> 00:26:10,416
You even had dinner with them
on your birthday. I was so happy that day.

390
00:26:11,416 --> 00:26:13,041
You're not alone anymore.

391
00:26:14,125 --> 00:26:18,250
If,

392
00:26:19,416 --> 00:26:21,507
something ever happens to me,

393
00:26:21,718 --> 00:26:25,291
you have Ji Hu now, and your brothers too.

394
00:26:25,625 --> 00:26:27,625
That gives me such peace of mind.

395
00:26:28,708 --> 00:26:30,541
Nothing like that will happen.

396
00:26:31,873 --> 00:26:34,956
Mom, you're getting pretty well-known
as a model now, aren't you?

397
00:26:34,986 --> 00:26:36,486
Of course.

398
00:26:36,916 --> 00:26:41,791
I'm starting a whole new chapter,
so don't get in my way, okay?

399
00:26:42,166 --> 00:26:43,625
Please.

400
00:26:46,375 --> 00:26:47,375
Mom.

401
00:26:47,662 --> 00:26:52,958
I heard when I was little, I'd put on
your dress and say I'd marry Dad.

402
00:26:53,583 --> 00:26:54,791
You did.

403
00:26:56,500 --> 00:26:58,416
You were so adorable.

404
00:27:00,750 --> 00:27:02,559
I miss Dad.

405
00:27:06,386 --> 00:27:09,136
I know. I miss him too.

406
00:27:17,333 --> 00:27:20,623
Ji Ni, why are you taking
your mom's clothes out?

407
00:27:20,625 --> 00:27:24,333
Na Ji Ni, I just finished
getting those clothes altered.

408
00:27:24,666 --> 00:27:28,000
Put this on me. I'm getting married.

409
00:27:28,041 --> 00:27:29,083
Getting married?

410
00:27:29,125 --> 00:27:32,041
I'm going to wear this and marry you, Dad.

411
00:27:32,083 --> 00:27:34,125
Look at her.

412
00:27:34,916 --> 00:27:37,083
Ji Ni, you want to marry me?

413
00:27:38,291 --> 00:27:41,527
You're supposed to wear a dress
when you get married.

414
00:27:41,675 --> 00:27:43,291
That's what the fairy tale books say.

415
00:27:45,458 --> 00:27:49,125
Ji Ni, your dad already married me.

416
00:27:49,541 --> 00:27:51,746
Dad, you're married?

417
00:27:51,900 --> 00:27:54,291
Then you can't marry me?

418
00:27:55,666 --> 00:27:57,041
No, let's get married.

419
00:27:57,083 --> 00:28:00,207
Come on, let's get married.
You and me, Ji Ni.

420
00:28:00,208 --> 00:28:03,875
- Come stand right here.
- Let's have the wedding march, please.

421
00:28:03,916 --> 00:28:07,208
One, two. How lovely!

422
00:28:16,333 --> 00:28:18,292
So pretty!

423
00:28:19,190 --> 00:28:22,375
My daughter should wear a veil
when she gets married.

424
00:28:22,416 --> 00:28:25,021
You shouldn't do it as I did.

425
00:28:26,250 --> 00:28:31,208
Okay, look over here.

426
00:28:50,573 --> 00:28:53,865
(Family Register)

427
00:28:53,916 --> 00:28:55,625
I'm always stuck in unrequited love.

428
00:28:55,666 --> 00:28:58,750
Ji Ni's always turning them down.
Don't you think that's unfair?

429
00:28:58,791 --> 00:29:00,625
Love isn't first come, first served.

430
00:29:00,666 --> 00:29:02,166
So cutting in line is allowed, then?

431
00:29:02,208 --> 00:29:03,583
That's him, right?
The boy from the accident?

432
00:29:03,625 --> 00:29:04,875
When did you get hurt?

433
00:29:04,925 --> 00:29:06,050
Why are you here?

434
00:29:06,083 --> 00:29:08,125
Looks like your daughter's husband
is doing pretty well.

435
00:29:08,166 --> 00:29:10,291
Go near my daughter, and I'll kill you.

436
00:29:10,333 --> 00:29:12,750
Everyone's gathered here.
Want me to make a real scene?

437
00:29:13,580 --> 00:29:15,580
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
